# Grok Build first (tier 1)

OpenSesame Cloud Agents use a **three-tier coding chain** (see also
`.cursor/rules/kimi-first.mdc` for tier 2). **All implementation edits go
through tier 1 while Grok Build quota allows.** The Cursor agent orchestrates:
plan, review, test, provenance, and PRs — it does not hand-write product code
while tier 1 is available.

## Tier 1 — Grok Build CLI

1. On agent start, install subscription auth with
   `bash scripts/dev/grok-install-subscription-auth.sh` (from
   `/cursor/stores/bot/grok/auth.json` to `~/.grok/auth.json`).
2. Run `scripts/dev/agent-coding-preflight.sh` (or `scripts/dev/grok-preflight.sh`
   plus `scripts/dev/grok-resolve-model.sh`) before batch coding.
3. Resolve the model: `scripts/dev/grok-resolve-model.sh` prints the pin
   (`grok-4.7` minimum; use a newer id from `grok models` when listed).
4. Always delegate coding through `scripts/dev/grok-headless.sh`. It unsets
   `XAI_API_KEY`, `GROK_CODE_XAI_API_KEY`, and `GROK_DEPLOYMENT_KEY`:

   ```bash
   model="$(scripts/dev/grok-resolve-model.sh)"
   scripts/dev/grok-headless.sh -p "<task>" -m "$model" --always-approve --output-format json
   ```

5. **Auth:** subscription login only. Install from
   `/cursor/stores/bot/grok/auth.json` via `grok-install-subscription-auth.sh`
   on agent start. **Never** use `XAI_API_KEY` for Grok Build. A set API key,
   or an API 403/credits response, is misconfiguration: unset the key and use
   the subscription file.

## When to leave tier 1 (tier 2 or 3)

Fall back to tier 2 only when `grok` itself reports a subscription **weekly
limit** or **quota**. Do not treat an API key 403 or a credits error as
tier-1 exhaustion — that is misconfiguration (unset the key and use
subscription auth). Then use **Kimi Code CLI (tier 2)** per `kimi-first.mdc`.
When Kimi is also exhausted, use **Cursor (tier 3)** — Grok 4.7 for security
testing and red-team work; Composer / auto for everything else.

Record the tier used and why in the PR **Provenance** section and
`docs/audit/2026-10-provenance.md` when material.
